{
  "program": "CBTRN02C",
  "caseId": "case13",
  "description": "An empty daily-transaction file read against a full set of collateral data, which is this folder's proof of the '10' end-of-file outcome and of the program's do-nothing baseline. THE EMPTY DECLARATION. DALYTRAN is declared empty rather than omitted: \"empty\": true carrying its recordLength 350 and its copybook CVTRA06Y, which is the only shape ParityCase.DatasetInput accepts for a dataset that exists and holds no row - an omitted key would say nothing about the dataset at all and an empty \"rows\" list is refused outright, and only the declaration reaches the branch a unit takes when its first READ meets end-of-file (practice B1). THE CHAIN. The READ at :346 reports '10', so the middle arm of the ordered ladder at :347-356 moves 16 into APPL-RESULT rather than the 0 of '00' or the 12 of anything else; 88 APPL-EOF is then true at :360 and :361 moves 'Y' into END-OF-FILE. CBTRN02C declares exactly two condition names - APPL-AOK VALUE 0 at :143 and APPL-EOF VALUE 16 at :144 - and this is the only case in the folder that drives the second one true. Back in the mainline the inner IF END-OF-FILE = 'N' at :205 is now false, so ADD 1 TO WS-TRANSACTION-COUNT at :206, 1500-VALIDATE-TRAN at :210, 2000-POST-TRANSACTION at :212, ADD 1 TO WS-REJECT-COUNT at :214 and 2500-WRITE-REJECT-REC at :215 never execute at all: the loop body is skipped in its entirety and the PERFORM UNTIL at :202 ends on its first pass with nothing counted, validated, posted or rejected (practice B11). WHAT STILL RUNS. All six OPEN paragraphs at :195-200 and all six CLOSE paragraphs at :221-226 still run, every one reporting FileStatus '00', and not one of them displays anything on success - the boundary of the loop is not an error and nothing about the program is simplified away on the strength of its input being empty (practice B5). THE RETURN CODE. WS-REJECT-COUNT is 0, so the guard at :229 is false and MOVE 4 TO RETURN-CODE at :230 - the only MOVE to RETURN-CODE anywhere in the program - does not fire, leaving 0. APPL-RESULT 16 is an internal loop signal and is never moved to RETURN-CODE, so the expected code is 0 and emphatically neither 12 nor 16; that is the easiest mis-translation on this path. NO TIMESTAMP. Z-GET-DB2-FORMAT-TIMESTAMP is performed only at :437, inside 2000-POST-TRANSACTION, so no TRAN-PROC-TS is composed anywhere on this path and the case is deterministic without depending on the pinned clock at all (practice B7). THE COLLATERAL IS SEEDED ON PURPOSE. XREFFILE, ACCTFILE and TCATBALF each carry their whole fixture - all 50 cross-reference rows, all 50 accounts and all 50 category balances - although the run reads none of them, because that is what makes the do-nothing outcome attributable to the empty DALYTRAN rather than to collateral the case forgot to supply. cardxref.txt is seeded at its literal 36 bytes and never pre-padded (gate G16); the declared CARDXREF_FILLER_PAD_36_TO_50 supplies CVACT03Y's absent FILLER PIC X(14) as 14 spaces once, at seed time. THE EXPECTATION CONVENTION. FieldDiffer compares each channel as a complete set in both directions and the suite reports every one of the five relations on the FINAL_STATE channel with every row it holds, so an untouched dataset has to be asserted rather than left out: every seeded row is pinned by its whole image, which is why 150 expectations appear here for a run that writes nothing. All 50 account rows keep their trailing FILLER X(178) of spaces and all 50 category balances keep the 22 zero characters the fixture carries in CVTRA01Y's FILLER X(22), so the widths hold end to end (gates G19 and G21). TRANFILE and DALYTRAN hold no row afterwards and DALYREJS was opened and written to not at all - app/jcl/POSTTRAN.jcl:34 declares DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE), which catalogues that as an empty 430-byte generation rather than as no generation - and each of those three is asserted as a dataset-level row count of zero, the one statement no row expectation can make. THE COUNT LINES. Both are still displayed, and both render nine zero-filled digits because WS-TRANSACTION-COUNT and WS-REJECT-COUNT are each PIC 9(09) VALUE 0 at :185-186; a bare 0 or a space-padded field would be wrong. The spacing before each colon is the source's own: one space in 'TRANSACTIONS PROCESSED :' at :227 and two in 'TRANSACTIONS REJECTED  :' at :228 (practice B8). The list is exactly four lines: '10' is an expected, silent status, so no ERROR READING DALYTRAN FILE, no FILE STATUS IS line from 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS, no ABENDING PROGRAM and no TCATBAL-record-not-found line appears. RELATION TO case16. case16 reaches the same branch with one row seeded into each collateral dataset; this case reaches it at the fixtures' full volume and pins all 150 rows, so it is also the cheapest smoke test in the folder - if dataset seeding, message capture or counter rendering is wrong anywhere, this case says so first and every sibling fails for the same reason. PROVENANCE. Every expected value here is statically derived by structured reading of app/cbl/CBTRN02C.cbl cross-checked against app/cpy/CVTRA06Y.cpy, CVTRA01Y.cpy, CVACT01Y.cpy and CVACT03Y.cpy, app/jcl/POSTTRAN.jcl and the app/data/ASCII fixtures - it is not captured from a COBOL execution, which the environment cannot perform (practice B12).",
